{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793533605,"nonce":"OvPyLX5+izsRuROZUvfJbWG6p5Q=","message":"Audit 2026-11-01 (read-only, before building). Verdict: BUILD SMALLER.\nVERIFIED blockers in the ticket as written:\n- Dogfood sets no Forgejo webhook secret (up.sh:530-532), so /webhooks/forgejo is disabled there (scarab-server lib.rs:131).\n- Bind registers the hook at {public_url}/webhooks/forgejo (lib.rs:9827, 10751); dogfood's publicUrl is the Cloudflare hostname (up.sh:545), so delivery would leave the cluster through the tunnel — not \"in-cluster, no tunnel\". Only e2e mode points publicUrl at the in-cluster Service (up.sh:533-537).\n- `on: cron:` parses (event.rs:58) but nothing schedules it (pipeline lib.rs:9566), so a CronJob is the only driver today.\n- Retention never prunes Run metadata (config.rs:55, main.rs:414); TTLs are 30d/90d/14d, so a one-day soak cannot show retention; a gate left pending makes a permanent non-terminal Run per tick.\nWould catch: slow server/Depot memory growth over hours (docker stats on the node, as chaos.sh:146 does); long-lived-cluster drift (ba32d49). Would not catch: Depot eviction (busybox steps never near the 2 GiB warm budget), retention, lease renewal, Reruns/Takes (human actions).\nRisks: until 070d042 is fixed, canary failures mostly measure laptop sleep.\nSimpler: a CronJob that curls POST /v1/repos/{org}/{repo}/dispatch (lib.rs:1884) — no webhook, secret or tunnel (check that dispatch can select a light pipeline). Longer term: a scheduler for `on: cron:`, which demo-keepalive.yml would also use.\nMinimal acceptance: a canary Run at least every 30 min while awake; every Run terminal (no pending gate); a docker-stats memory sample per tick and an 8 h awake soak with no monotonic growth (numbers recorded); Runs spanning a recorded sleep tagged and excluded until 070d042 is fixed; leaving dogfood removes the CronJob; retention either 1-day TTLs + a